   WITHDRAWN 2026-09-20: an earlier version of this file explained the table by
   'each constraint removes about a quarter, so survivors ~ e*(3/4)^6'. That is an
   independent-density estimate. It is banned by MANUSCRIPT §6A row six, and it is
   also REFUTED -- Appendix A routes 10-14 measured the joint density BELOW the
   product of the pairwise conditionals (ratio to 0.716, 2594/3000 profiles), so the
   constraints anti-correlate and the estimate is wrong as well as inadmissible.

   What stands, exactly and without density:
     * flank e has exactly e openings                     (Theorem 15H)
     * for d < e,  c_d = e/gcd(d,e) = m  <=>  d = j*e/m, gcd(j,m)=1;
       in particular  c_d = 2  <=>  e/2 is itself a disparity   (checked, 0 mismatches)
     * a witness at e exists iff the CRT system {k mod c_d in A_d} is solvable
   The table above is a MEASUREMENT of association between min c_d and failure.
   It is not an explanation, and nothing here derives the failure rate.
